# rm — paideia-as build products
#
# `build-out/` is populated by `paideia-as build` (via tools/build.sh
# in the parent paideia-os repo). Each build produces:
#   build-out/rm         -- the elaborated .pdx -> ELF-like Paideia binary
#   build-out/rm.caps    -- the caps.decl copy the loader consumes
# plus any per-source .o intermediates the incremental build keeps.
# None of these belong in git; the .release/ tree carries the signed
# tarball produced by `paideia-as release --sign`.

build-out/
